{
  "_comment": "Continuous time of day (world/sky/sky_cycle.gd). sun / moon: arcs keyed by game minute (azimuth from north clockwise, the overworld camera looks north). keys: colour keys interpolated linearly between their times (wrapping at midnight). A key MODULATES the zone's look, it never replaces it: colours lerp from the zone's own value by their *_weight, *_energy / exposure / sky_ambient multiply the zone's value; 12:30 is the identity (zone look as authored). lamps / windows feed the night_lamps / night_windows shader globals and NightLights; stars / haze drive the sky shader; sky_neutral (at least the look's metadata/sky_neutral) pulls the sky light (ambient, SDFGI, reflections) toward the key's ambient colour, so grey stone in shadow does not turn blue; shafts / fireflies the old ambience. fill: a shadowless light from behind the camera that tops up the moon while the sun is down (energy at no moon), so sprites and the facades the camera sees stay readable in the twilight gaps. periods: the hour each forced period (--period=<id>) shows. Tune live with the F9 sky panel.",
